(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-09-02"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-09-02","label":"2026 年 9 月 2 日","date":"2026-09-02","range":"","theme":"经济学","themes":["经济学"],"sources":["BARRON’S"],"title":"Feeding AI: Data From A Bankrupt Airline","titleZh":"","counts":{"article":0,"paragraph":19,"vocab":37,"question":15,"qa":0,"original":3,"layout":0},"tabs":{"articles":false,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[],"reading":[{"file":"9.2 精读(1).pdf","headline":{"title":"Feeding AI: Data From A Bankrupt Airline","titleZh":"","source":"BARRON’S","series":"考研那些事儿之经济学系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"The race to build the most advanced artificial-intelligence tools has spawned a new market for real world data. It comes with both opportunities and pitfalls for investors.","zh":"围绕开发最先进人工智能工具的竞争催生了现实数据这一新市场。这对投资者而言既蕴含机遇，也暗藏风险。"},{"index":2,"en":"Earlier this month, Google won an auction to purchase Spirit Airlines’ software code, internal messages, and financial and operational data for $10 million, according to filings from Spirit’s bankruptcy proceedings. Google hopes to use the data to improve its products and AI models, a spokesperson said.","zh":"据Spirit航空公司破产程序的文件显示，本月早些时候，谷歌在拍卖中以1000万美元的价格竞得Spirit航空公司的软件代码、内部通信以及财务和运营数据。谷歌一位发言人表示，该公司希望利用这些数据来改进其产品和人工智能模型。"},{"index":3,"en":"That $10 million outlay for a busted airline’s data is just the tip of the iceberg. AI companies are vacuuming up corporate information of all sorts—a process that has taken on greater importance now that scraping the internet has become more legally fraught.","zh":"一家破产航空公司的数据能卖出1000万美元，这还只是冰山一角。人工智能公司正在大量吸纳各类企业信息——随着从互联网上抓取数据在法律上变得越来越棘手，这一过程如今变得愈发重要。"},{"index":4,"en":"The demand for data is linked to how AI large-language models are created and refined. The computer systems ingest huge volumes of human information and use it to mimic human processes, such as writing reports, interpreting and responding to messages, and making recommendations. More data means more examples the model can pull from.","zh":"对数据的需求与人工智能大型语言模型的构建和优化密切相关。计算机系统会摄入海量的人类信息，并利用这些信息模拟人类的处理流程，例如撰写报告、解读和回复消息以及提供建议。数据越多，模型可借鉴的样本就越多。"},{"index":5,"en":"In response, public companies are weighing whether to license their data. And start-ups are opening marketplaces through which smaller enterprises can sell everything from contracts to email threads.","zh":"作为回应，上市公司正在权衡是否要授权其数据。而初创企业则正在开设交易平台，让小型企业能够通过这些平台出售从合同到电子邮件往来记录等各类数据。"},{"index":6,"en":"“Companies are sitting on decades of records that show how real work gets done, and that data is now some of the most valuable material for training and evaluating AI,” said a spokesperson from Mercor, an AI data start-up that made a $7.5 million bid in the Spirit auction.","zh":"“企业掌握着数十年的记录，这些记录展示了实际工作是如何完成的，而这些数据如今已成为训练和评估人工智能的最有价值的素材之一，”人工智能数据初创公司Mercor的一位发言人表示。该公司在Spirit的拍卖中出价750万美元。"},{"index":7,"en":"The economics make perfect sense. The five largest cloud providers are spending a combined $800 billion in capital expenditures in 2026 to build data centers, and AI labs are paying hundreds of billions to use the facilities. Millions of dollars—with an “M”—mean very little to them when creating new AI tools, but that money can be a game-changer for data sellers.","zh":"从经济角度来看，这完全合乎逻辑。五大云服务提供商在2026年合计投入8000亿美元资本，用于建设数据中心，而人工智能实验室也在支付数千亿美元来使用这些设施。对于开发新的人工智能工具而言，数百万美元——这里指的是“M”开头的百万——对它们来说微不足道，但这笔钱却可能彻底改变数据卖家的命运。"},{"index":8,"en":"The market appears to be picking up. In January, Cloudflare acquired HumanNative, a marketplace connecting content creators with AI developers. Two months later, News Corp, the owner of Barron’s publisher Dow Jones, struck a licensing deal with Meta Platforms, where the publisher sold access to its content for $50 million a year.","zh":"这一市场似乎越发火热。今年1月，Cloudflare收购了HumanNative——这是一个将内容创作者与AI开发者连接起来的市场平台。两个月后，《巴伦周刊》出版商道琼斯（隶属于新闻集团）与MetaPlatforms达成了一项许可协议，该出版商以每年5000万美元的价格出售其内容的访问权限。"},{"index":9,"en":"For smaller companies and even individuals looking to sell their data, an array of start-ups are emerging to broker deals.","zh":"对于希望出售数据的小型公司甚至个人而言，一批初创企业正应运而生，致力于促成相关交易。"},{"index":10,"en":"Over a recent 11-day stretch, micro1, an AI data venture, committed more than $20 million to license operational data, said CEO Ali Ansari in a social media post this past week.","zh":"人工智能数据初创公司micro1的首席执行官阿里·安萨里（AliAnsari）上周在社交媒体上发文称，在最近的11天内，该公司已承诺投入超过2000万美元用于获取运营数据的授权。"},{"index":11,"en":"Investors can get in on the action, too. Barron’s made two stock picks last month based on the growing value of AI training data.","zh":"投资者也可以参与其中。《巴伦周刊》上个月基于人工智能训练数据价值的不断增长，推荐了两只股票。"},{"index":12,"en":"Reddit struck agreements with OpenAI and Google in 2024 to license conversations from its forums, bringing in an estimated $60 million a year from each lab. The social-media platform is now in negotiations with Google, and some investors and analysts expect a much larger deal.","zh":"Reddit于2024年与OpenAI和谷歌达成协议，授权其使用论坛中的对话数据，预计从每家实验室每年可获得6000万美元收入。该社交媒体平台目前正与谷歌进行谈判，部分投资者和分析师预计将达成一笔规模更大的交易。"},{"index":13,"en":"John Wiley & Sons, a publisher of academic and technical literature, has also racked up big-name customers. The company’s licensing agreements with leading AI developers have generated more than $110 million since 2024. It also has collaborations with Amazon Web Services, Microsoft, Anthropic, and others.","zh":"学术与技术文献出版商约翰·威利父子公司（JohnWiley&Sons）也已积累了众多知名客户。自2024年以来，该公司与领先的人工智能开发商达成的授权协议已创收超过1.1亿美元。此外，它还与亚马逊网络服务（AWS）、微软、Anthropic等公司建立了合作关系。"},{"index":14,"en":"The key for investors, and indeed companies, is pinpointing when data sales may do more harm than good.","zh":"对投资者乃至企业而言，关键在于准确判断数据销售何时会弊大于利。"},{"index":15,"en":"Privacy is one challenge, particularly for consumer-facing businesses. Opera, the Norwegian web-browser company, has resisted selling data on those grounds.","zh":"隐私是一个挑战，特别是对于面向消费者的企业而言。挪威网络浏览器公司Opera正是基于这些理由，一直拒绝出售用户数据。"},{"index":16,"en":"“If we lose the users’ trust, if they think, ‘Oh, if we use the Opera browser, then they’re actually going to sell our data,’ then it’s probably not a wise move,” said Frode Jacobsen, chief financial officer at Opera, at an investor conference in January.","zh":"“如果我们失去了用户的信任，如果他们认为‘哦，如果我们使用Opera浏览器，他们实际上就会出售我们的数据’，那么这可能并不是一个明智之举，”Opera首席财务官弗罗德·雅各布森（FrodeJacobsen）在今年1月的一次投资者大会上表示。"},{"index":17,"en":"Disruption by AI is the other threat. If the labs use a company’s proprietary information to build something better, or at least more popular, they could siphon away demand.","zh":"人工智能带来的颠覆是另一项威胁。如果这些实验室利用公司的专有信息开发出更优秀、或者至少更受欢迎的产品，它们可能会分流需求。"},{"index":18,"en":"“Our data is really the crown jewels of the future,” said Gary Morrison, CEO of hostel booking platform Hostelworld Group, in a conference call last month. “It is everything that we know about profiles, about bookings, about events, about people you’re meeting, what you’re talking about.”","zh":"“我们的数据确实是未来的‘皇冠明珠’，”青年旅舍预订平台HostelworldGroup的首席执行官加里·莫里森在上个月的一次电话会议上表示。“这包括我们所掌握的一切：用户画像、预订信息、活动详情、客户将结识的人，以及客户谈论的话题。”"},{"index":19,"en":"But companies like Hostelworld, and indeed Reddit and John Wiley, will have to survive in an AI-dominated world whether they like it or not. That means many more executives will have to decide how much “the crown jewels” are worth.","zh":"但像Hostelworld这样，乃至Reddit和约翰·威利（JohnWiley）这样的公司，无论愿意与否，都必须在人工智能主导的世界中生存下去。这意味着将有更多高管不得不去判断这些“皇冠明珠”究竟价值几何。"}],"vocab":[{"term":"bankrupt","head":"a. without enough money to pay what you owe SYN insolvent They went bankrupt in 1993.","definition":"without enough money to pay what you owe SYN insolvent They went bankrupt in 1993.","gloss":"破产；倒闭他们于 1993 年破产。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"race","head":"n. ~ (for sth/to do sth) a situation in which a number of people, groups, organizations, etc. are competing, especially for political power or to achieve sth first","definition":"~ (for sth/to do sth) a situation in which a number of people, groups, organizations, etc. are competing, especially for political power or to achieve sth first","gloss":"竞争；角 逐 the race for the presidency 总统竞选","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇","️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"spawn","head":"v. (often disapproving) to cause sth to develop or be produced The band's album spawned a string of hit singles.","definition":"(often disapproving) to cause sth to develop or be produced The band's album spawned a string of hit singles.","gloss":"引发；引起；导致；造成这支乐队的专辑繁衍出一连串走红的单曲唱片。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"pitfall","head":"n. a danger or difficulty, especially one that is hidden or not obvious at first the potential pitfalls of buying a house","definition":"a danger or difficulty, especially one that is hidden or not obvious at first the potential pitfalls of buying a house","gloss":"危险；困难；（尤指）陷阱，隐患购买房屋可能遇到的圈套","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"auction","head":"n. a public event at which things are sold to the person who offers the most money for them an auction of paintings","definition":"a public event at which things are sold to the person who offers the most money for them an auction of paintings","gloss":"拍卖【️考研大纲词汇】绘画拍卖会","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大 纲词汇"]},{"term":"filing","head":"n. the act of putting documents, letters, etc. into a file record a bankruptcy filing","definition":"the act of putting documents, letters, etc. into a file record a bankruptcy filing","gloss":"存档；归档 something that is placed in an official存档档案；归档记录破产档案","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"proceeding","head":"n. (formal) [C, usually pl.]~ (against sb) (for sth) the process of using a court to settle a disagreement or to deal with a complaint bankruptcy/divorce/extradition, etc. proceedings","definition":"(formal) [C, usually pl.]~ (against sb) (for sth) the process of using a court to settle a disagreement or to deal with a complaint bankruptcy/divorce/extradition, etc. proceedings","gloss":"诉讼；诉讼程序破产、离婚、引渡等诉讼","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"spokesperson","head":"n. (pl.-persons or -people) ~ (for sb/sth)a person who speaks on behalf of a group or an organization","definition":"(pl.-persons or -people) ~ (for sb/sth)a person who speaks on behalf of a group or an organization","gloss":"发言人","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"outlay","head":"n. ~ (on sth) the money that you have to spend in order to start a new project（ The business quickly repaid the initial outlay on advertising.","definition":"~ (on sth) the money that you have to spend in order to start a new project（ The business quickly repaid the initial outlay on advertising.","gloss":"启动新项目的）开支，费用这家公司很快偿付了初期的广告费。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"busted","head":"a.","definition":"","gloss":"破产的","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"the tip of the iceberg idiom only","head":"a. small part of a much larger problem（","definition":"small part of a much larger problem（","gloss":"问题的）冰山一角","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"vacuum","head":"v. If you vacuum something, you clean it using a vacuum cleaner.","definition":"If you vacuum something, you clean it using a vacuum cleaner.","gloss":"用真空吸尘器清洁","example":"I vacuumed the carpets today.","exampleZh":"我今天用吸尘器清洁地毯了。","tags":[]},{"term":"take on","head":"phrase. If something takes on a new appearance or quality, it develops that appearance or quality.","definition":"If something takes on a new appearance or quality, it develops that appearance or quality.","gloss":"呈现","example":"Believing he had only a year to live, his writing took on a feverish intensity.","exampleZh":"他认为自己只有一年能活了，他的文字呈现出一种极度的狂热。","tags":[]},{"term":"scrap","head":"v. [often passive] to cancel or get rid of sth that is no longer practical or useful They had been forced to scrap plans for a new school building.","definition":"[often passive] to cancel or get rid of sth that is no longer practical or useful They had been forced to scrap plans for a new school building.","gloss":"废弃；取消；抛弃；报废他们已被迫撤销了建筑新校舍的计划。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"fraught","head":"a. causing or feeling worry and anxiety SYN tense She looked/sounded fraught.","definition":"causing or feeling worry and anxiety SYN tense She looked/sounded fraught.","gloss":"焦虑的；忧虑的；担心的她愁容满面；她的话音显出忧虑。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"refine","head":"v. If something such as a process, theory, or machine is refined, it is improved by having small changes made to it.","definition":"If something such as a process, theory, or machine is refined, it is improved by having small changes made to it.","gloss":"完善","example":"Surgical techniques are constantly being refined.  ingest v. When animals or plants ingest a substance, they take it into themselves, by eating or absorbing it. ...side effects occurring in fish that ingest this substance. ...","exampleZh":"外科手术技术正在不断得到完善。摄取; 吸收在吃了此物质的鱼身上产生的副作用。","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"volume","head":"n. The volume of something is the amount of it that there is.","definition":"The volume of something is the amount of it that there is.","gloss":"量","example":"Senior officials will be discussing how the volume of sales might be reduced.  interpret v. If you interpret something in a particular way, you decide that this is its meaning or significance. The fact that they had decided to come was interpreted as a positive sign.","exampleZh":"高级官员们将讨论如何才能减少销售量。解释【️考研大纲词汇】他们已经决定要来的事实可被解释为一个积极的信号。","tags":["️考研大纲词汇","️考 研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"weigh","head":"v. If you weigh the facts about a situation, you consider them very carefully before you make a decision, especially by comparing the various facts involved.","definition":"If you weigh the facts about a situation, you consider them very carefully before you make a decision, especially by comparing the various facts involved.","gloss":"权衡【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"She weighed her options.","exampleZh":"她在各种选择间权衡斟酌。","tags":["️考 研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"start-up","head":"n. a company that is just beginning to operate, especially an Internet company","definition":"a company that is just beginning to operate, especially an Internet company","gloss":"刚成立的公司，新企业（尤指互联网公司）","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"thread","head":"n. (computing on a message board on the Internet which have been sent by different people（","definition":"(computing on a message board on the Internet which have been sent by different people（","gloss":"计) a series of connected messages互联网留言板上帖子的）系列相关信息，链式消息","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"bid","head":"n. ~ (for sth) an offer by a person or a business company to pay a particular amount of money for sth At the auction (= a public sale where things are sold to the person who offers most) , the highest bid for the picture was ￡200.","definition":"~ (for sth) an offer by a person or a business company to pay a particular amount of money for sth At the auction (= a public sale where things are sold to the person who offers most) , the highest bid for the picture was ￡200.","gloss":"买方的出价拍卖会上，这幅画的最高出价为 200 英镑。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"expenditure","head":"n. the act of spending or using money; an amount of money spent a reduction in public/government/military expenditure ╱","definition":"the act of spending or using money; an amount of money spent a reduction in public/government/military expenditure ╱","gloss":"花费；消费；费用；开支公共政府╱军费开支的削减","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"game changer","head":"n. a newly introduced element or factor that changes an exisiting situation or activity in a significant way","definition":"a newly introduced element or factor that changes an exisiting situation or activity in a significant way","gloss":"新出现的能影响整个局势的变量","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"pick up","head":"phrase. If trade or the economy of a country picks up, it improves. (","definition":"If trade or the economy of a country picks up, it improves. (","gloss":"贸易、经济) 改善","example":"Industrial production is beginning to pick up.","exampleZh":"工业生产正在开始好转。","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"strike","head":"v. to make an agreement with sb in which both sides have an advantage","definition":"to make an agreement with sb in which both sides have an advantage","gloss":"达成（对双方都有利的）协议【️考研大纲词汇】","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词 汇"]},{"term":"array","head":"n. [usually sing.] a group or collection of things or people, often one that is large or impressive a vast array of bottles of different shapes and sizes","definition":"[usually sing.] a group or collection of things or people, often one that is large or impressive a vast array of bottles of different shapes and sizes","gloss":"大堆；大群；大量一大批形状大小不一的瓶子","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"emerge","head":"v. ~ (as sth) to start to exist; to appear or become known After the elections opposition groups began to emerge.","definition":"~ (as sth) to start to exist; to appear or become known After the elections opposition groups began to emerge.","gloss":"露头；显现；显露经过选举，反对派开始露头。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"stretch","head":"n. a continuous period of time（ SYN spell They worked in four-hour stretches.","definition":"a continuous period of time（ SYN spell They worked in four-hour stretches.","gloss":"连续的）一段时间他们工作四小时一班。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"commit","head":"v. to spend money or time on sth/sb","definition":"to spend money or time on sth/sb","gloss":"花（钱或时间） The council has committed large amounts of money to housing projects. 市政会在住宅项目上投入了大量资金。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇","️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"negotiation","head":"n. [usually pl. U] formal discussion between people who are trying to reach an agreement peace/trade/wage, etc. negotiations","definition":"[usually pl. U] formal discussion between people who are trying to reach an agreement peace/trade/wage, etc. negotiations","gloss":"谈判；磋商；协商和谈、贸易洽谈、工资谈判等","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"rack up","head":"phrase. If a business racks up profits, losses, or sales, it makes a lot of them. If a sportsman, sportswoman, or team racks up wins, they win a lot of games or races.","definition":"If a business racks up profits, losses, or sales, it makes a lot of them. If a sportsman, sportswoman, or team racks up wins, they win a lot of games or races.","gloss":"大量获得 (利润); 严重遭受 (损失); (体育中) 多次赢得 (比赛)","example":"Lower rates mean that firms are more likely to rack up profits in the coming months.","exampleZh":"更低的费率意味着各公司更有可能在未来的几个月里获得大量利润。","tags":[]},{"term":"big-name","head":"a.","definition":"","gloss":"知名的；出名的","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"pinpoint","head":"v. to find and show the exact position of sb/sth or the exact time that sth happened","definition":"to find and show the exact position of sb/sth or the exact time that sth happened","gloss":"明确指出，确定（位置或时 间） He was able to pinpoint on the map the site of the medieval village. 他能在地图上准确找出那个中世纪村庄的位置。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"ground","head":"n. for sth/for doing stha good or true reason for saying, doing or believing sth","definition":"for sth/for doing stha good or true reason for saying, doing or believing sth","gloss":"充分的理由；根据 The case was dismissed on the grounds that there was not enough evidence. 此案以缺乏足够的证据为由被驳回。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词 汇","️考研大纲词 汇"]},{"term":"proprietary","head":"a. [usually before noun] (of goods protected by a registered trademark a proprietary medicine","definition":"[usually before noun] (of goods protected by a registered trademark a proprietary medicine","gloss":"商品) made and sold by a particular company and专卖的；专营的；专利的专卖药品","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"siphon","head":"v. (informal) to remove money from one place and move it to another, especially dishonestly or illegally（ SYN divert She has been accused of siphoning off thousands of pounds from the company into her own bank account.","definition":"(informal) to remove money from one place and move it to another, especially dishonestly or illegally（ SYN divert She has been accused of siphoning off thousands of pounds from the company into her own bank account.","gloss":"尤指私自或非法）抽走，转移（钱）她被指控把公司的几千英镑转移到了自己的账户里。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"profile","head":"n. a description of sb/sth that gives useful information","definition":"a description of sb/sth that gives useful information","gloss":"概述；简介；传略 a job/employee profile 工作╱雇员简介","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["️考研大纲词汇","️考研大纲词汇"]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】9.2 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 1 to 3, Google's purchase of Spirit Airlines' data is presented as _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a legal settlement required by Spirit's bankruptcy proceedings"},{"key":"B","text":"evidence that airlines now earn more from software than from passengers"},{"key":"C","text":"an early sign that real-world corporate data have become a valuable AI market"},{"key":"D","text":"proof that internet scraping is no longer necessary for AI development"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·开篇例证识别","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 1-3","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：The race to build the most advanced artificial-intelligence tools has spawned a new market for real world data.","- 原文（Para.2）：Earlier this month, Google won an auction to purchase Spirit Airlines' software code, internal messages, and financial and operational data for $10 million...","- 原文（Para.3）：That $10 million outlay for a busted airline's data is just the tip of the iceberg. AI companies are vacuuming up corporate information of all sorts...","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。数据来自破产程序文件，但 Google 是 auction 中购得，不是法院要求的法律和解。","- 选项B（错误）：无中生有陷阱。原文没有比较航空公司软件收入与客运收入。","- 选项C（正确）：首段先提出 real world data 新市场，再用 Google 以 1,000 万美元购买破产航空公司数据作例证；第三段进一步称这只是 iceberg 的顶端。","- 选项D（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文说网络抓取更法律风险，导致企业数据重要性上升，不是 AI 开发已完全不需要网络数据。","【命题技巧】","- 开篇例证功能：个案价值要看它服务的第一段观点，而不是只复述交易细节。","- 因果强度核对：more legally fraught 不等于 scraping 已经完全不必要。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 4 to 7 that corporate records attract AI developers partly because _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"public companies are legally required to put all contracts and email threads on sale"},{"key":"B","text":"large cloud providers have stopped building data centres to avoid capital spending"},{"key":"C","text":"smaller enterprises can now obtain bankruptcy assets without participating in auctions"},{"key":"D","text":"such records provide rich examples of real work while buyers' vast spending makes million-dollar prices bearable"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·商业动因推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 4-7","【解析】","- 原文（Para.4）：The computer systems ingest huge volumes of human information and use it to mimic human processes...More data means more examples the model can pull from.","- 原文（Para.6）：“Companies are sitting on decades of records that show how real work gets done, and that data is now some of the most valuable material for training and evaluating AI.”","- 原文（Para.7）：The five largest cloud providers are spending a combined $800 billion in capital expenditures in 2026...Millions of dollars...mean very little to them...but that money can be a game-changer for data sellers.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：无中生有陷阱。上市公司在 weighing whether to license data，没有被法律强制出售所有合同和邮件。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。五大云服务商 2026 年资本开支合计约 8,000 亿美元，不是停止建设数据中心。","- 选项C（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。小企业可以通过市场出售数据，但原文没有说它们能不参加拍卖即获得破产资产。","- 选项D（正确）：企业记录展示 real work gets done，为模型训练和评估提供大量真实样本；同时买方资本开支巨大，数百万美元对它们影响很小。D 项合并了数据价值和买方承受力两条动因。","【命题技巧】","- 供需两侧合并：数据质量解释为什么有价值，买方支出解释为什么价格可承受。","- 数字规模对比：$800 billion 与 millions with an M 的反差是本段修辞重点。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"Which of the following is true about the market examples in Paragraphs 8 to 13?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"John Wiley & Sons has generated more than $110 million from AI licensing agreements since 2024."},{"key":"B","text":"Cloudflare licensed its own web users' personal data to HumanNative in January."},{"key":"C","text":"micro1 committed just over $2 million to operational-data licences over 11 days."},{"key":"D","text":"Reddit has signed deals with OpenAI and Google worth an estimated $16 million a year from each lab."}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·正误判断","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 8-13","【解析】","- 原文（Para.8）：In January, Cloudflare acquired HumanNative, a marketplace connecting content creators with AI developers.","- 原文（Para.10）：Over a recent 11-day stretch, micro1...committed more than $20 million to license operational data...","- 原文（Para.12）：Reddit struck agreements with OpenAI and Google in 2024 to license conversations from its forums, bringing in an estimated $60 million a year from each lab.","- 原文（Para.13）：John Wiley & Sons...The company's licensing agreements with leading AI developers have generated more than $110 million since 2024.","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：Para.13 明确说明 Wiley 与领先 AI 开发者的授权协议自 2024 年以来产生超过 1.1 亿美元收入，并涉及 AWS、Microsoft、Anthropic 等。","- 选项B（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。Cloudflare acquired HumanNative，即收购连接内容创作者和 AI 开发者的市场平台，不是出售自家用户个人数据给它。","- 选项C（错误）：数字偷换陷阱。micro1 在 11 天里承诺超过 2,000 万美元，不是刚超过 200 万美元。","- 选项D（错误）：数字偷换陷阱。Reddit 与 OpenAI 和 Google 的协议估计分别为每年 6,000 万美元，不是 1,600 万美元。","【命题技巧】","- 交易方向核对：收购平台、出售数据、授权内容三类交易容易被互换。","- 数字精确配对：$20m、$60m、$110m 都需与主体和时间归属一致。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"The author uses the examples of Opera and Hostelworld in Paragraphs 15 to 18 to show that data sellers must _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"follow Opera's example and sell consumer data as quickly as possible"},{"key":"B","text":"treat proprietary data as worthless once AI products enter their markets"},{"key":"C","text":"weigh possible revenue against user trust and the risk of strengthening AI competitors"},{"key":"D","text":"ignore investor concerns and preserve every internal record for future litigation"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】作者态度题·风险权衡","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 15-18","【解析】","- 原文（Para.15）：Privacy is one challenge, particularly for consumer-facing businesses. Opera...has resisted selling data on those grounds.","- 原文（Para.16）：“If we lose the users' trust, if they think, ‘Oh, if we use the Opera browser, then they're actually going to sell our data,' then it's probably not a wise move.”","- 原文（Para.17）：Disruption by AI is the other threat. If the labs use a company's proprietary information to build something better, or at least more popular, they could siphon away demand.","- 原文（Para.18）：“Our data is really the crown jewels of the future...It is everything that we know about profiles, about bookings, about events, about people you're meeting, what you're talking about.”","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Opera has resisted selling data，它不是尽快出售消费者数据的榜样。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。Hostelworld 称 data 是 crown jewels，说明数据极具战略价值，不是一文不值。","- 选项C（正确）：作者先列 privacy 与用户信任风险，再列 AI disruption：出售数据可能让实验室构建更有竞争力的产品并分流需求。例子共同说明数据销售需要在收益、信任和竞争风险之间权衡。","- 选项D（错误）：无中生有陷阱。原文没有建议为了诉讼保存所有内部记录，投资者关注的是数据出售的利弊。","【命题技巧】","- 两类风险并列：privacy/trust 与 AI disruption 构成例证功能的双主线。","- 战略资产隐喻：crown jewels 强调数据既可出售获利，也可能削弱长期竞争力。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Bankruptcy Bargains: Why Failed Airlines Are the Only Source of AI Data"},{"key":"B","text":"Feeding AI: Corporate Data Become Valuable Assets but Not Risk-Free Sales"},{"key":"C","text":"Privacy First: Why No Responsible Company Should Ever License Data"},{"key":"D","text":"Data Pipelines: How Small Start-ups Ended the Power of Cloud Giants"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：The race to build the most advanced artificial-intelligence tools has spawned a new market for real world data. It comes with both opportunities and pitfalls for investors.","- 原文（Para.7）：...that money can be a game-changer for data sellers.","- 原文（Para.14）：The key for investors, and indeed companies, is pinpointing when data sales may do more harm than good.","- 原文（Para.19）：That means many more executives will have to decide how much “the crown jewels” are worth.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：过度推理陷阱。Spirit 是开篇例子，后文还有 Reddit、Wiley、News Corp、smaller firms 等多种数据来源，不是唯一来源。","- 选项B（正确）：全文先说明 AI 训练催生 real world data 市场，再列举交易和商业机会，最后转向隐私信任与 AI 竞争风险。B 项同时概括“有价值”和“有代价”，对应首段 opportunities and pitfalls。","- 选项C（错误）：过度推理陷阱。作者讨论隐私风险，但不是主张任何负责任公司都永不授权数据；许多授权交易被呈现为商业机会。","- 选项D（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。创业公司主要充当中介或买家，五大云服务商的巨额资本开支和议价影响力仍是市场背景。","【命题技巧】","- 首尾观点闭环：首段 opportunities and pitfalls 与尾段 crown jewels 定价共同确定文章边界。","- 例证宽度判断：标题不能被 Spirit 个案或 Opera 的谨慎立场窄化。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】9.2检验题__完型填空(1).docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["Earlier this month, Google won an auction to purchase Spirit Airlines’ software code, internal messages, and financial and operational data for $10 million, according to filings from Spirit’s bankruptcy proceedings. Google ____【11】____ to use the data to ____【12】____ its products and AI models, a spokesperson said.","That $10 million ____【13】____ for a busted airline’s data is just the tip of the iceberg. AI companies are ____【14】____ up corporate information of all sorts—a process that has taken on greater ____【15】____ now that scraping the internet has become more legally ____【16】____.","The demand for data is ____【17】____ to how AI large-language models are created and refined. The computer systems ____【18】____ huge volumes of human information and use it to mimic human processes, such as writing reports, interpreting and responding to messages, and making recommendations. More data means more ____【19】____ the model can pull from.","In response, public companies are weighing whether to license their data. And start-ups are opening ____【20】____ through which smaller enterprises can sell everything from contracts to email threads.","“Companies are sitting on decades of records that show how real work gets done, and that data is now some of the most valuable material for training and evaluating AI,” said a spokesperson from Mercor, an AI data start-up that made a $7.5 million bid in the Spirit auction."],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"hopes"},{"key":"B","text":"refuses"},{"key":"C","text":"hesitates"},{"key":"D","text":"pretends"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (refuses)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·意图语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] refuses（拒绝）：与 Google 购买数据后的用途矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] hopes（希望）：Google hopes to use the data 表示谷歌希望使用这些数据。正确答案。","[C] hesitates（犹豫）：语义可通，但没有证据说明其不确定。语义场干扰。","[D] pretends（假装）：带负面判断且与发言人说明事实不符。感情色彩干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"monitor"},{"key":"B","text":"replace"},{"key":"C","text":"improve"},{"key":"D","text":"standardise"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (improve)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·动宾搭配","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] monitor（监测）：可搭配 products，但不能说明 AI models 获得训练提升。语义场干扰。","[B] replace（替代）：文意是优化产品，不是替代产品。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] improve（改进）：improve its products and AI models 表示“改进产品和 AI 模型”。正确答案。","[D] standardise（标准化）：与提升模型能力的语境偏离。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"outlay"},{"key":"B","text":"refund"},{"key":"C","text":"deposit"},{"key":"D","text":"discount"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (outlay)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·金融语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] outlay（支出）：outlay for... data 表示为数据支付的款项。正确答案。","[B] refund（退款）：钱是谷歌付出，不是收回。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] deposit（押金）：拍卖成交款不是保证金。语义场干扰。","[D] discount（折扣）：语义偏离，未涉及原价比较。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"adding"},{"key":"B","text":"giving"},{"key":"C","text":"taking"},{"key":"D","text":"vacuuming"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (vacuuming)","analysis":["【题型】动词短语·形象语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] adding（增加）：adding up 多指计算总数，不是大量收集。近义干扰。","[B] giving（给出）：give up 表示放弃，方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] taking（拿取）：taking up 可表示开始从事，与大规模吸取数据有别。搭配干扰。","[D] vacuuming（吸取、吸取式收集）：vacuuming up corporate information 形象表示大量吸走企业信息。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"importance"},{"key":"B","text":"accuracy"},{"key":"C","text":"secrecy"},{"key":"D","text":"delay"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (accuracy)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·抽象语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] accuracy（准确性）：信息收集过程本身不等于准确性提高。语义场干扰。","[B] importance（重要性）：taken on greater importance 表示“变得更重要”。正确答案。","[C] secrecy（保密性）：法律争议使获取数据更受关注，不是更秘密。语义场干扰。","[D] delay（延误）：与过程重要性上升不对应。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fraught"},{"key":"B","text":"profitable"},{"key":"C","text":"popular"},{"key":"D","text":"straightforward"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (fraught)","analysis":["【题型】形容词辨析·法律语境","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] fraught（充满风险的）：legally fraught 表示法律上充满风险，与网络抓取变得更麻烦呼应。正确答案。","[B] profitable（有利可图的）：若更赚钱，企业未必转向企业数据。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] popular（受欢迎的）：语义偏社交接受度，不体现法律麻烦。语义场干扰。","[D] straightforward（简单直接的）：方向相反，不能推动企业寻找其他数据来源。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"linked"},{"key":"B","text":"separated"},{"key":"C","text":"protected"},{"key":"D","text":"exaggerated"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (linked)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·逻辑关系","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第1句","【解析】","[A] linked（相关）：is linked to 表示数据需求与大模型创建和改进方式相关。正确答案。","[B] separated（分离）：与后文模型依赖大量信息矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] protected（保护）：保护数据不是此处解释需求来源。语义场干扰。","[D] exaggerated（夸大）：文段在解释机制，不是评价说法是否夸大。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"discard"},{"key":"B","text":"publish"},{"key":"C","text":"weigh"},{"key":"D","text":"ingest"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (ingest)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·数据语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第2句","【解析】","[A] discard（丢弃）：丢弃信息与后文 use it to mimic human processes 矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] publish（公开）：模型吸收数据不等于公开发布。语义场干扰。","[C] weigh（权衡）：权衡信息与吸收大量信息不同。语义场干扰。","[D] ingest（摄取）：The computer systems ingest huge volumes... 表示计算机系统摄取大量人类信息。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rules"},{"key":"B","text":"examples"},{"key":"C","text":"rivals"},{"key":"D","text":"warnings"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (examples)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·上下文语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 3, 第3句","【解析】","[A] rules（规则）：模型可学习规律，但原文明确说 examples the model can pull from。原文对应干扰。","[B] examples（例子）：更多数据意味着模型可提取的例子更多。正确答案。","[C] rivals（竞争者）：与模型学习人类信息无关。语义场干扰。","[D] warnings（警告）：无法说明数据量带来的训练价值。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"laboratories"},{"key":"B","text":"archives"},{"key":"C","text":"marketplaces"},{"key":"D","text":"agencies"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (marketplaces)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·商业功能","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 4, 第2句","【解析】","[A] laboratories（实验室）：不能直接提供交易渠道。语义场干扰。","[B] archives（档案库）：存储数据不等于促成买卖。语义场干扰。","[C] marketplaces（市场）：opening marketplaces 与 smaller enterprises can sell 形成买卖平台关系。正确答案。","[D] agencies（机构）：可泛指服务组织，但不如 marketplaces 与 sell everything 精确对应。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"9.2 精读(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":700638,"date":"2026-09-02","range":"","title":"Feeding AI: Data From A Bankrupt Airline","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\9.2 精读(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.2 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":58192,"date":"2026-09-02","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.2 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】9.2检验题__完型填空(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":61110,"date":"2026-09-02","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】9.2检验题__完型填空(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
